<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa's Autonet year profit edges up.</title>
<headline>S.Africa's Autonet year profit edges up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Profit for the year   22.9	 vs  20.1</p>
<p>    Operating profit	20.7	 vs  18.0</p>
<p>    Net finance income     2.2	 vs   2.1</p>
<p>    Turnover		 431.0	 vs 399.0</p>
<p>    Transnet costs	  11.1	 vs  15.3</p>
<p>    Retained profit	 11.8	 vs   4.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Autonet is the passenger and road transportation division of South African transport parastatal Transnet.</p>
<p>Government recently announced that it had earmarked transport as the second sector to be assessed for privatisation following its assessment of the telecommunications sector.</p>
<p>Peter Mageza, acting chief executive of Autonet, said the company would ensure operating profit of 24 million rand in the 1996/97 financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
